# A unified diff carries the whitespace of the file it patches, so the whitespace checks have to be
# switched off for these: a blank context line IS a single space, and a context line of tab-indented
# C IS a space followed by a tab. "Cleaning" either one stops the patch applying, which is why the
# exemption lives here rather than in the patches themselves.
#
# Both patterns cover files that already had these characters; only the check is new. The Zephyr
# driver patches are listed for the same reason as the vendored ULD ones, so that touching either
# kind later does not start reporting a defect that would break the patch if anyone fixed it.
patches/zephyr/*.patch -whitespace
lexxpluss_apps/third_party/st/*/zephyr/patches/*.patch -whitespace
